@startuml
left to right direction

actor Client
database ClientPod
node Auctioneer
queue EventQueue
node "Bidder (PITAS application)" as BidderApp {
  node "pitas-auction-house" as BidderAH
  node "pitas-worker-pool" as WorkerPool
  node "pitas-jobs +\npitas-scheduler" as BidderJobs
}
control Worker
database WorkerPod

' Minimum deployment that satisfies the two sovereignty rules of Exercise 9:
'   Rule 1: task input and result stay in the ClientPod; Auctioneer, Bidder
'           and Worker only pass links and keep no copy.
'   Rule 2: worker details stay in the WorkerPod; the Bidder keeps only the
'           Worker's WebID.
' "Auction house" in Rule 2 is the whole Bidder application: as in the groups'
' code (E7/E8), the Worker registers with the worker pool, the auction house
' only reads it, and a won job goes through pitas-jobs and the scheduler to
' the Worker; the auction house never calls the Worker directly.
' Auctions, bids, and awards are not covered by the rules; here they travel
' as messages and stay in the applications (no further pods).
' Permission grants are left out.
' Timing: only step 8 is placed by a rule. Rule 2 makes the Bidder resolve
' worker details "at run time ... whenever it needs them", so it fetches them
' per auction. Step 7 could happen at any time (the Bidder may keep WebIDs);
' it comes before step 8 only because the WebID is needed to reach the pod.
' Layout: Client and Auctioneer left, Bidder and Worker right, queue in
' between. Arrows are written left to right (with <-- for the reverse flow)
' to keep the columns; parallel messages share one arrow, numbers give the
' order. Worker setup (1.-2.) comes before the task.

Client --> ClientPod : 3. write task input\n25. read task result
Client --> Auctioneer : 4. commission task (link to input)
Client <-- Auctioneer : 24. notify task done (link to result)

Auctioneer --> EventQueue : 5. push auction event\n13. push award event
Auctioneer <-- EventQueue : 11. deliver sealed bid\n23. deliver result event
Auctioneer --> Auctioneer : 12. evaluate bids

EventQueue --> BidderAH : 6. deliver auction event\n14. deliver award event
EventQueue <-- BidderAH : 10. push sealed bid (Worker WebID)\n22. push result event (link to result)
BidderAH --> WorkerPool : 7. fetch registered Worker WebIDs
BidderAH --> WorkerPod : 8. fetch worker details
BidderAH --> BidderAH : 9. evaluate auction
BidderAH --> BidderJobs : 15. hand over won job (links only)\n21. poll job status

WorkerPool <-- Worker : 1. register (WebID only)
Worker --> WorkerPod : 2. write worker details
BidderJobs --> Worker : 16. dispatch (links only)
BidderJobs <-- Worker : 20. report execution done
ClientPod <-- Worker : 17. fetch task input\n19. append task result
Worker --> Worker : 18. execute (no copy kept)

@enduml
